{"id": "tea:srikantha-bhasya:1.1.2", "source": "src:srikantha-bhasya", "location": {"ref": "1.1.2"}, "paraphrase": "On 'that from which the birth etc. of this (world) proceed': that cause is Parameśvara Śiva, who with his cit-śakti is both the material and the efficient cause of the world.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:srikantha"], "concepts": ["cpt:siva-visistadvaita"], "terms": ["trm:cit-sakti"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:srikantha-bhasya:1.3.14", "source": "src:srikantha-bhasya", "location": {"ref": "1.3.14"}, "paraphrase": "The small space (dahara) within the lotus of the heart (Chāndogya 8.1) is Brahman — Śiva as the supreme ether (paramākāśa), which is his cit-śakti — and is the object of the dahara meditation.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate", "practice"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:srikantha"], "concepts": ["cpt:dahara-siva"], "practices": ["prc:dahara-vidya"], "terms": ["trm:dahara", "trm:paramakasa"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:srikantha-bhasya:2.2.38", "source": "src:srikantha-bhasya", "location": {"ref": "2.2.38"}, "paraphrase": "Śrīkaṇṭha declares that he sees no difference between the Veda and the Śivāgama: both are authoritative as coming from Śiva; what the sūtras reject is only a view of the Lord as merely the efficient cause.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "polemical", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["dispute", "teacher-transmission"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:srikantha"], "concepts": ["cpt:veda-agama-equality"], "disputes": ["dsp:authority-of-the-agamas", "dsp:status-of-veda"], "notes": "Adhikaraṇa BS 2.2.37–41 (patyuḥ); sūtra-level locus of the statement to verify.", "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:srikantha-bhasya:4.4.17", "source": "src:srikantha-bhasya", "location": {"ref": "4.4.17"}, "paraphrase": "The released soul attains all the Lord's powers except the activity of the world (creation, maintenance, dissolution): it becomes equal to Śiva in bliss and knowledge, not identical with him.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "ultimate"], "coverage": ["A6"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U16-bhedabheda"], "disagreements": []}, "teachers": ["tch:srikantha"], "concepts": ["cpt:siva-samya", "cpt:moksa"], "terms": ["trm:siva-samya"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U16-bhedabheda"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
